course: dictionary
lesson: 15113
title: Salade, the French word for salad
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Salade» is a French word, not an English one. It means salad, or lettuce, and it sounds like «sa-LAD» to English ears. You will see it on menus in English-speaking places, so it is useful to know.
explain: «Je mange une salade verte au déjeuner.» Here salade is a noun, a naming word for something you can eat. The little word «une» comes before it and means one. Context helps: «verte» means green, so this is a green salad.
explain: The words after salade give you clues about which salad it is. «Salade niçoise» has tuna, egg, olives and green beans in it, so you can guess it is a full meal salad. Always check your guess by reading the words around it.
fact: «Salade» is a French noun, so it comes with a little word before it: «une salade» means one salad, and «des salades» means some salads.
fact: «Salade» means salad or lettuce in French.
fact: «Salade verte» means green salad, and «salade de fruits» means fruit salad.
fact: «Salade niçoise» is a salad from Nice, with tuna, egg, olives and green beans.
fact: In informal French, «quelle salade!» can mean «what a mess!», so always check the context before you translate it.
exercise: «Je voudrais une salade verte, s'il vous plaît.» What does salade mean here? | Soup | A plate | Bread | *Salad, or lettuce
exercise: On a café menu, Mia sees «salade de fruits». What is it? | *Fruit salad | Dried fruit | Fruit tart | Fruit juice
exercise: «Salade niçoise» is on the menu. What is it? | *A salad with tuna, egg, olives and green beans | A cake with cream | A sandwich with cheese and ham | A soup with carrots and peas
test: In informal French, what does «quelle salade!» mean? | Please pass the salt | Well done for cooking | It is very hot today | *What a mess!
test: «Une salade» means one salad. What does «des salades» mean? | A lettuce leaf | One big salad | *Some salads | A salad bowl
exam: Which phrase on the menu means green salad? | *salade verte | salade niçoise | salade de fruits | soupe de légumes
